tps://www.beatlesbible.com/1999/03/18/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-universal-amphitheatre-los-angeles-2/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Universal Amphitheatre, Los Angeles</a></li><li>1996: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1996/03/18/album-release-anthology-2/\">Album release: Anthology 2</a></li><li>1977: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1977/03/18/recording-b-side-to-seaside-suzy-and-the-red-stripes-3/\">Recording: B Side To Seaside by Suzy And The Red Stripes</a></li><li>1976: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1976/03/18/press-launch-wings-at-the-speed-of-sound/\">Press launch for Wings At The Speed Of Sound</a></li><li>1976: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1976/03/18/jim-mccartney-dies/\">Jim McCartney dies</a></li><li>1975: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1975/03/18/cover-photoshoot-venus-and-mars-wings/\">Cover photoshoot: Venus And Mars by Wings</a></li><li>1973: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1973/03/18/wings-live-hard-rock-cafe-london/\">Wings live: Hard Rock Cafe, London</a></li><li>1972: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1972/03/18/recording-mixing-sisters-o-sisters-the-luck-of-the-irish-angela-woman-is-the-n-r-of-the-world-born-in-a-prison-john-lennon-yoko-ono/\">Recording, mixing: Sisters, O Sisters, The Luck Of The Irish, Angela, Woman Is The N****r Of The World, Born In A Prison by John Lennon and Yoko Ono</a></li><li>1971: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1971/03/18/recording-too-many-people-ram-on-paul-linda-mccartney/\">Recording: Too Many People, Ram On by Paul and Linda McCartney</a></li><li>1969: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/03/18/george-pattie-harrison-appear-in-court-drugs-charges/\">George and Pattie Harrison appear in court on drugs charges</a></li><li>1968: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1968/03/18/us-single-lady-madonna/\">US single release: Lady Madonna</a></li><li>1965: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1965/03/18/lennon-mccartney-jam-obertauern-austria/\">Lennon and McCartney jam in Obertauern, Austria</a></li><li>1965: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1965/03/18/filming-help-20/\">Filming: Help!, Austria</a></li><li>1964: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1964/03/18/radio-the-public-ear-3/\">Radio: The Public Ear</a></li><li>1964: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1964/03/18/filming-a-hard-days-night-13/\">Filming: A Hard Day’s Night</a></li><li>1963: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1963/03/18/live-regal-cinema-gloucester/\">The Beatles live: Regal Cinema, Gloucester</a></li><li>1962: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1962/03/18/live-casbah-coffee-club-liverpool-32/\">The Beatles live: Casbah Coffee Club, Liverpool</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div><div class=\"gm-map\" style=\"position: relative;height: 390px; width: 100%;\"><iframe data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"about:blank\" name=\"gm-map-1\" allowfullscreen=\"\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/?geo_mashup_content=render-map&amp;map_data_key=2d898a4da6fe7f7b347a9d06fa09b4b2&amp;height=390&amp;width=100%&amp;add_overview_control=false&amp;zoom=16&amp;enable_street_view=false&amp;map_type=G_HYBRID_MAP&amp;name=gm-map-1&amp;object_id=133405&amp;map_content=single\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; overflow: hidden;\" title=\"Geo Mashup Map\"></iframe></div>",
  "textContent": "Filming for the television special James Paul McCartney continued on 18 March 1973 at Elstree Studios. This was the only day of filming to feature all the members of Wings. They had taken part in two days of rehearsals in February and March, but the rest of the filming featured only Paul and Linda McCartney.The day was spent filming a concert sequence. On 8 March a letter had been sent to members of the Wings Fun Club, inviting them to apply for free tickets for the concert.The show began at 7.45pm. The set included ‘The Long And Winding Road’, ‘Maybe I’m Amazed’, ‘When The Night’, ‘The Mess’, ‘Wild Life’, ‘Go Now’, ‘Hi, Hi, Hi’, and ‘Long Tall Sally’.Due to technical issues, Wings performed two sets. The second ended at 10pm, and included two versions of ‘Hi, Hi, Hi’, but omitted ‘Long Tall Sally’.Produced by ATV, James Paul McCartney was first broadcast on 16 April 1973 in the USA, and 10 May in the UK. It was released on DVD as part of the super deluxe reissue of in Red Rose Speedway December 2018.\n\n\n\n\n\nPage last updated: 28 November 2025Also on this day...1999: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Universal Amphitheatre, Los Angeles1996: Album release: Anthology 21977: Recording: B Side To Seaside by Suzy And The Red Stripes1976: Press launch for Wings At The Speed Of Sound1976: Jim McCartney dies1975: Cover photoshoot: Venus And Mars by Wings1973: Wings live: Hard Rock Cafe, London1972: Recording, mixing: Sisters, O Sisters, The Luck Of The Irish, Angela, Woman Is The N****r Of The World, Born In A Prison by John Lennon and Yoko Ono1971: Recording: Too Many People, Ram On by Paul and Linda McCartney1969: George and Pattie Harrison appear in court on drugs charges1968: US single release: Lady Madonna1965: Lennon and McCartney jam in Obertauern, Austria1965: Filming: Help!, Austria1964: Radio: The Public Ear1964: Filming: A Hard Day’s Night1963: The Beatles live: Regal Cinema, Gloucester1962: The Beatles live: Casbah Coffee Club, LiverpoolWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
